And even with that, I've seen more MC-less ascensions than MR-less.
Every naked ascension is MC-less; most of them have MR from an
artifact.  I've only seen 2 MR-less ascensions.

MC3 is generally a good idea, but since there aren't any MC-blockable
instadeaths it's not nearly as important as MR.  Going MR-less almost
mandates wearing "oLS and taking special precautions to avoid other
nasty effects (e.g. =polycontrol and quaffing !hallucination at points
where you know touch of death is a reasonable probability).

Going MC-less entails taking the kinds of precautions that you'd
normally want anyway (keeping lizard corpses around, having ways of
purifying lycanthropy)--and given that MC3 isn't 100% effective, it's
unsurprising that you want those precautions normally even with MC3.
The biggest headache is level-drain, but judicious use of Elbereth can
protect against that pretty well (and once you've alchemized a bit, you
need to be drained of more than 3 levels to lose one permanently I
believe--potions of full healing will restore some fraction of lost
levels, and killing the first monster after draining buys a level as
well).



